    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0747" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> A.E.C. Files (Historical Doc. No. 166)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Director of the Office of
                        Scientific Research and Development</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bush</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d325-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-20">July 20, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Van</hi>: While the Prime Minister was here we
                    discussed the whole question of exchange of information regarding <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Tube Alloys</hi>, including the building
                    project.</p>
                <p>While I am mindful of the vital necessity for security in regard to this, I feel
                    that our understanding with the British encompasses the complete exchange of all
                    information.</p>
                <p>I wish, therefore, that you would renew, in an inclusive manner, the full
                    exchange of information with the British Government regarding <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Tube Alloys</hi>.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d325-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d325-f1-content">
                <p>This letter was delivered to Busies office in Washington while Bush was in
                    England, and he was informed of its contents by cable. Concerning the garble in
                    the message as he received it, see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg645">p. 645</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
